---
// Lo stesso profilo con una scarpata netta, rappresentato da un TIN e da un raster.
// I gradini del raster sono calcolati campionando il centro di ogni cella.
---

<figure class="my-8">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 700 275" role="img" aria-labelledby="tin-title" class="h-auto w-full text-foreground">
    <title id="tin-title">
      Lo stesso profilo con una scarpata: il TIN infittisce i vertici sul salto e lo riproduce netto,
      il raster lo distribuisce su una cella e lo arrotonda a gradino.
    </title>

    <text x="190" y="46" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground">TIN</text>
    <text x="550" y="46" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground">raster · DEM</text>
    <polyline points="40,108 120,107 185,108 200,108 215,172 240,173 300,172 340,172" fill="none" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="2" />
    <circle cx="40" cy="108" r="3.5" class="fill-foreground" />
    <circle cx="40" cy="210" r="2" class="fill-muted-foreground" />
    <circle cx="120" cy="107" r="3.5" class="fill-foreground" />
    <circle cx="120" cy="210" r="2" class="fill-muted-foreground" />
    <circle cx="185" cy="108" r="3.5" class="fill-foreground" />
    <circle cx="185" cy="210" r="2" class="fill-muted-foreground" />
    <circle cx="200" cy="108" r="3.5" class="fill-foreground" />
    <circle cx="200" cy="210" r="2" class="fill-muted-foreground" />
    <circle cx="215" cy="172" r="3.5" class="fill-foreground" />
    <circle cx="215" cy="210" r="2" class="fill-muted-foreground" />
    <circle cx="240" cy="173" r="3.5" class="fill-foreground" />
    <circle cx="240" cy="210" r="2" class="fill-muted-foreground" />
    <circle cx="300" cy="172" r="3.5" class="fill-foreground" />
    <circle cx="300" cy="210" r="2" class="fill-muted-foreground" />
    <circle cx="340" cy="172" r="3.5" class="fill-foreground" />
    <circle cx="340" cy="210" r="2" class="fill-muted-foreground" />
    <line x1="40" y1="210" x2="340" y2="210" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="1" />
    <text x="348" y="214" font-size="9.5" class="fill-muted-foreground">vertici</text>
    <polyline points="400,108 425,108 425,108 450,108 450,108 475,108 475,108 500,108 500,108 525,108 525,108 550,108 550,108 550,140 550,140 575,140 575,140 575,172 575,172 600,172 600,172 625,172 625,172 650,172 650,172 675,172 675,172 700,172" fill="none" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="2" />
    <polyline points="400,108 560,108 575,172 700,172" fill="none" class="stroke-muted-foreground" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
    <line x1="400" y1="94" x2="400" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="425" y1="94" x2="425" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="450" y1="94" x2="450" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="475" y1="94" x2="475" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="500" y1="94" x2="500" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="525" y1="94" x2="525" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="550" y1="94" x2="550" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="575" y1="94" x2="575" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="600" y1="94" x2="600" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="625" y1="94" x2="625" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="650" y1="94" x2="650" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="675" y1="94" x2="675" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <line x1="700" y1="94" x2="700" y2="186" class="stroke-border" stroke-width="0.7" />
    <text x="708" y="214" font-size="9.5" class="fill-muted-foreground">celle</text>
    <text x="190" y="242" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground">vertici densi dove la superficie cambia</text>
    <text x="190" y="260" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground">lo spigolo resta netto</text>
    <text x="550" y="242" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground">celle uniformi su tutta l'estensione</text>
    <text x="550" y="260" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground">lo spigolo si perde in una cella</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
    Il TIN ha risoluzione <strong class="font-medium text-foreground">variabile</strong>: dove la
    superficie è piatta bastano pochi vertici, dove cambia se ne mettono molti, e una discontinuità
    resta esattamente dove è. Il raster ha celle uniformi, quindi spende risoluzione anche dove non
    serve e non riesce a collocare il salto dentro una cella: il tratteggio è il profilo vero.
    La scelta si fa su questo — un argine, una scarpata o il bordo di una cava chiedono un TIN;
    terreno regolare ed esteso conviene raster, che costa molto meno.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
